---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="About Aawaz Pokhrel, PhD: pharma R&D partnerships, R&D program leadership, and imaging and AI for drug development."
  wide
>
  <header class="page-header">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p>I'm a PhD scientist who works where pharma R&amp;D meets the business. I build relationships with drug development teams, figure out what they're actually trying to solve, and turn that into scientific programs that get them to a decision.</p>
  </header>

  <!-- Currently at DigiM -->
  <section class="current-block">
    <div class="current-inner">
      <p class="block-kicker">Currently</p>
      <h2>Lead Application Scientist at <a href="https://www.digimsolution.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">DigiM</a></h2>
      <p class="current-body">
        I joined DigiM as a Senior Application Scientist in October 2024 and was promoted to Lead Application Scientist in April 2026. I lead the scientific relationship and growth strategy for several of DigiM's most strategic pharma accounts and the FDA, manage a team of scientists, and run 10–15 R&amp;D workstreams at a time.
      </p>
      <p class="current-body">
        I'm key investigator on DigiM's ~$5M FDA research contract, where I work with FDA scientists and directors to set research priorities and lead generative-AI work on drug product microstructure.
      </p>
      <p class="current-body">
        Since joining I've managed 200+ projects, and about 92% led to follow-on work. A lot of my job is discovery: finding out what a client's team is stuck on, scoping a study around it, and writing the scope of work and quote. My hands-on work covers long-acting injectables, peptide tablets and peptide LAIs, inhaled biologics, microspheres, implants, and oral solids. I also built an LLM-based reporting workflow that cut executive-summary prep from about 6 hours to 1, and the team uses it now.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- What I build -->
  <section class="build-section">
    <p class="section-kicker">What I build</p>
    <p class="build-intro">
      Outside of work I build things. Right now that means <strong>Paperika</strong>, a tool that takes your name or scholarly profile, infers your research area, and gives you a ranked feed of newly published papers in your field, with a relatedness verdict and a one-line rationale for each. It's a problem I ran into myself: I wanted to stay current without spending an hour every week sorting through everything that wasn't relevant.
    </p>
    <div class="build-card">
      <div class="build-card-inner">
        <p class="build-label">Live</p>
        <p class="build-name">Paperika</p>
        <p class="build-line">Hot papers in your field. A radar for papers that matter to your work.</p>
        <a href="https://paperika.aawazpokhrel.com" class="build-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Try Paperika →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    
  </section>

  <!-- Background -->
  <section class="bio-section">
    <p class="section-kicker">Background</p>
    <p class="bio-body">
      I did my PhD in Physics at Georgia Tech, studying how bacterial colonies grow. The work involved a lot of microscopy, image analysis, and building models and it led to a first-author paper in <em>Nature Physics</em> that was featured by <em>Quanta Magazine</em>. More than the result, what I took from that experience was a habit of asking whether the evidence actually supports what you're claiming. That's shaped how I think about everything since.
    </p>
    <p class="bio-body nepal-block">
      Before grad school, I ran a project through the <a href="https://nepalieducationforpeace.home.blog/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Davis Project for Peace</a> — a $10,000 grant I wrote and managed to set up three community libraries across two rural schools in Nepal. It was my first real experience leading something from an idea to something that existed in the world. I'm from Nepal originally, so this one was personal.
    </p>
    <div class="edu-list">
      <div class="edu-item">
        <span class="edu-year">2024</span>
        <span class="edu-text">PhD, Physics · Georgia Institute of Technology</span>
      </div>
      <div class="edu-item">
        <span class="edu-year">2020</span>
        <span class="edu-text">MS, Physics · Georgia Institute of Technology</span>
      </div>
      <div class="edu-item">
        <span class="edu-year">2019</span>
        <span class="edu-text">BS, Physics & Computer Science · Gettysburg College</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-header {
    padding: var(--space-12) 0 var(--space-8);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-10);
  }
  .page-header h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 2.6rem);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }
  .page-header p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    max-width: 52rem;
  }

  .block-kicker,
  .section-kicker {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent-ink);
    font-weight: 600;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-3);
  }

  /* Currently block */
  .current-block {
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent-soft) 48%, transparent);
    border-radius: 20px;
    padding: var(--space-8);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-12);
  }
  .current-inner h2 {
    font-size: 1.55rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-4);
  }
  .current-inner h2 a {
    color: var(--accent-ink);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 40%, transparent);
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }
  .current-inner h2 a:hover {
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  .current-body {
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--text);
    max-width: 54rem;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-4);
  }
  .current-body:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  /* Build section */
  .build-section {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-12);
  }
  .build-intro {
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
    max-width: 52rem;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-6);
  }
  .build-card {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
  }
  .build-card-inner {
    display: inline-block;
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 28%, var(--border));
    border-radius: 16px;
    padding: var(--space-6) var(--space-8);
    box-shadow: 0 4px 18px rgba(82, 54, 38, 0.08);
    max-width: 32rem;
  }
  .build-label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent-ink);
    background: var(--accent-soft);
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0.18rem 0.55rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-2);
  }
  .build-name {
    font-size: 2rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    color: var(--text);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-2);
  }
  .build-line {
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    line-height: 1.55;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-4);
  }
  .build-link {
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--accent-ink);
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .build-link:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
  .build-why {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    line-height: 1.68;
    max-width: 52rem;
    margin: 0;
    font-style: italic;
  }

  /* Background */
  .bio-section {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-12);
  }
  .bio-body {
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
    max-width: 52rem;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-4);
  }
  .nepal-block {
    border-left: 3px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, var(--border));
    padding-left: var(--space-4);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
  }
  .nepal-block a {
    color: var(--accent-ink);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
  }
  .edu-list {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    border-left: 2px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 22%, var(--border));
    padding-left: var(--space-4);
    margin-top: var(--space-6);
  }
  .edu-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: var(--space-4);
  }
  .edu-year {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    color: var(--accent-ink);
    font-weight: 600;
    min-width: 2.8rem;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }
  .edu-text {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

</style>
